      "problem": "If each cube represents $1$ cubic unit, what is the volume of the figure?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/2e9da7bdc1b3e20a197be4c7e2ab3a64abcbdd78dc16274bc314e73bdc6bd1ce.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The figure consists of $3$ rows, and each row has $5$ cubes.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/baa53ae50449e9d56821925d9fbe5d2ebf694badd4e1e5e3c604fdcbf698a16f.png)\n\nSo, there are $5 \\times 3 = 15$ cubes in total.\n\nTherefore, the volume of the figure is $15$ cubic units.",
